From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenWrt Builder <builder@openwrt.org>
Date: Sat, 9 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: mediatek: downgrade missing PHY LED pinctrl to
 warning

The Airoha AN7581 internal GbE PHY on the Gemtek XG2010G does not
connect the PHY LED controller to panel LEDs (they are driven via GPIO
LEDs).  In that case the optional "gbe-led" pinctrl state is not present
and the current driver logs an error.  Downgrade this to a warning since
the PHY continues to work normally.

---
 drivers/net/phy/mediatek/mtk-ge-soc.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/phy/mediatek/mtk-ge-soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/mediatek/mtk-ge-soc.c
@@ -984,7 +984,7 @@ static int mt7988_phy_probe(struct phy_de
 	/* Only now setup pinctrl to avoid bogus blinking */
 	pinctrl = devm_pinctrl_get_select(&phydev->mdio.dev, "gbe-led");
 	if (IS_ERR(pinctrl))
-		dev_err(&phydev->mdio.bus->dev,
+		dev_warn(&phydev->mdio.bus->dev,
 			"Failed to setup PHY LED pinctrl\n");
 
 	return 0;
@@ -1096,7 +1096,7 @@ static int mt7981_phy_probe(struct phy_
 	/* Toggle pinctrl to enable PHY LED */
 	pinctrl = devm_pinctrl_get_select(&phydev->mdio.dev, "gbe-led");
 	if (IS_ERR(pinctrl))
-		dev_err(&phydev->mdio.bus->dev,
+		dev_warn(&phydev->mdio.bus->dev,
 			"Failed to setup PHY LED pinctrl\n");
 
 	priv = devm_kzalloc(&phydev->mdio.dev, sizeof(*priv), GFP_KERNEL);
